<title>USA: Mississippi led states in tobacco battle.</title>
<headline>Mississippi led states in tobacco battle.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mississippi Attorney General Mike Moore in May 1994 became the first state legal officer to sue the tobacco industry to recoup the costs of treating smokers.</p>
<p>Many of his colleagues took similar action and some legal experts said that the state Medicaid suits, potentially the most damaging of all the cases against cigarette makers, helped spur the settlement talks. Following is a list of cases brought by the state officials and the dates they were filed:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>1) May 23, 1994 - Mississippi</p>
<p>2) June 2, 1994 - West Virginia</p>
<p>3) Aug. 17, 1994 - Minnesota</p>
<p>4) Feb. 22, 1995 - Florida</p>
<p>5) Dec. 19, 1995 - Massachusetts</p>
<p>6) March 13, 1996 - Louisiana</p>
<p>7) March 28, 1996 - Texas</p>
<p>8) May 1, 1996 - Maryland</p>
<p>9) June 5, 1996 - Washington State</p>
<p>10) July 18, 1996 - Connecticut</p>
<p>11) Aug. 20, 1996 - Kansas</p>
<p>12) Aug. 20, 1996 - Arizona</p>
<p>13) Aug. 21, 1996 - Michigan</p>
<p>14) Aug. 22, 1996 - Oklahoma</p>
<p>15) Sept. 10, 1996 - New Jersey</p>
